-- title:
--   Local-Slope Constants Extend To The Pre-Energy Test Family
-- statement:
--   This theorem transfers a local-slope Poincaré constant to the associated identity-weighted pre-energy test family.
--
--   Let $V$ be a finite-dimensional complete real inner-product normed space with its Borel measurable structure and second-countable topology. Let $\nu$ be a probability measure on $V$, let $m$ be an additive Haar measure, and assume
--
--   1. $\nu\ll m$;
--   2. $\nu(\partial\operatorname{supp}\nu)=0$;
--   3. for a constant $C\in[0,\infty)$ represented by `NNReal`, the predicate `Poincare.LocalSlope.Holds ν C` holds.
--
--   Then the same constant satisfies the test-family inequality for the pre-energy generated by the identity-weighted gradient operator:
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{TestFamily.Holds}\!\left(
--   \operatorname{TestFamily.ofPreEnergy}(\nu,
--   \operatorname{PreEnergy.ofLinearPMap}(\operatorname{WeightedGradient.operator}(\nu,\operatorname{id},\nu\ll m))),C
--   \right).
--   $$
--
--   The declaration is `holds_ofPreEnergy_of_localSlope`. It is a comparison result between two formally defined Poincaré predicates; it does not assert that such a constant exists or is finite.
-- source:
--   Lean source: https://github.com/human-ai-mathematics/kls-lean/blob/408915f/formalization/FunctionalInequalities/Poincare/LipschitzGradient/Comparison.lean#L64-L90 (repository human-ai-mathematics/kls-lean, commit 408915f, module `FunctionalInequalities.Poincare.LipschitzGradient.Comparison`, declaration `FunctionalInequalities.Energy.LipschitzGradient.holds_ofPreEnergy_of_localSlope`; the repository is private at upload time).

